    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Time fetched:</b> Oct 6, 2026 6:12AM EDT</p><h2>LIVE CONDENSATION</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/condensation/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Condensation-favorability index 0-100 (DERIVED from HRRR analysis, fixed absolute scale): <b>LOWEST 0</b> tan dry &rarr; yellow &rarr; green &rarr; teal favorable &rarr; blue very favorable &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 100</b> deep-blue saturated. Same index always shows the same color. Saturation closeness from depression plus humidity — not relative humidity renamed, not dew point renamed, no fog visibility gate.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km 2 m TMP+DPT+RH analysis, hourly cycles (derived condensation-favorability index)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
